      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Between 1810 and 1814, the town—then called Nieuwer-Amstel—served as the capital of a French canton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amstelveen",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Today Amstelveen hosts the international headquarters of KLM and KPMG, two of the world’s largest companies.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amstelveen",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Cobra Museum, devoted to contemporary art, is a cultural landmark within Amstelveen.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amstelveen",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "An electric tram line still connects Amstelveen to Amsterdam, winding past the Amsterdamse Bos and the Olympic rowing lake.",
